  "seven_q": {
    "Q0_posture": "Critical and analytical; the document examines an isomorphism claim with rigorous testing and honest assessment.",
    "Q1_identity": "An isomorphism record (ISO-022) that maps the Lowe Coherence Lagrangian (LLC) to Christian theology's unity of truth.",
    "Q2_domain": "Physics/Mathematics and Christian Theology, with strong philosophical and information theory components.",
    "Q3_claim": "The ten laws of the framework, when expressed as a coupled Lagrangian system with specific symmetry pairs, structurally instantiate the theological claim that all truth is unified because it derives from one God.",
    "Q4_support": "Conceptual mapping between Lagrangian mechanics (unity generating multiplicity, symmetry, Noether's theorem) and theological concepts (divine simplicity, creation, coherence). The Information-Entropy pairing has independent physics support.",
    "Q5_dependencies": "The LLC must be a genuine Lagrangian (satisfying Euler-Lagrange equations); the symmetry pairs must be mathematically justified; the ten laws must be independent; the pairing must not be numbering-dependent.",
    "Q6_consequences": "If confirmed, it provides a formal instantiation of 'all truth is God's truth' and motivates cross-domain predictions. If falsified, it collapses to an analogy.",
    "Q7_kill": "Showing the LLC is not a real Lagrangian (e.g., no generalized coordinates, no Euler-Lagrange derivation); showing symmetry pairs are numbering-dependent; showing any ten items can be paired this way; theological voluntarism that denies necessary unified law."
  },
